          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 267889,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Thanks for sharing. Looking at A1, what's the difference between the 'Special Handling Surcharge' and the 'Dangerous Goods Fee' accounts? They seem similar.",
            "mentions": [
              333646
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 345866,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "I had the same question. Also, are we getting rid of the old 'Misc Costs' account completely?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 254387,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Good question. My take is that 'Special Handling' could be for things like fragile art or temperature-controlled items, while 'Dangerous Goods' is specifically for statutorily defined hazardous materials. We need to be very clear on that to avoid mis-postings. The descriptions in A1 should probably spell that out.",
            "mentions": [
              267889
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 456000,
            "reply_to": "M4",
            "text": "Exactly. We need to track dangerous goods separately for compliance. I'll add more explicit descriptions to A1. And yes, the old 'Misc Costs' is being replaced by more specific accounts to improve our job costing.",
            "mentions": [
              254387,
              345866
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 449944,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "Looking at the direct costs section in A1, we should consider splitting 'Transport Costs'. Right now it's a single account. For long-haul vs. local moves, the cost structure is very different. Having separate accounts would give us better visibility on profitability per job type. This also impacts how we'd structure the job costing template later.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "thinking_face",
                "count": 1
