        "thread_id": "TH2",
        "thread_goal": "Define and finalise the relocation accounting SOP, including handover.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M20",
            "speaker_id": 456000,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Hi all, following our approval of the chart of accounts, I've drafted the full 'Relocation Accounting SOP' in A2. It covers the end-to-end posting flow (T2) and includes a proposal for the data handover from operations (T12). Please review and provide feedback.",
            "mentions": [
              254387,
              267889,
              333646,
              345866,
              449944
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "T2",
              "T12"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M21",
            "speaker_id": 345866,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "Thanks. I'm reading through it. In section 3, does the job costing sheet need to be completed before we raise the final invoice?",
            "mentions": [
              456000
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M22",
            "speaker_id": 333646,
            "reply_to": "M21",
            "text": "Good question. The SOP draft says yes. We need the final costs to ensure the invoice is accurate and we capture everything. The goal is to avoid issuing credit notes later.",
            "mentions": [
              345866
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M23",
            "speaker_id": 254387,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "The section on dangerous goods is a good start, but we should explicitly state what documentation needs to be attached to the transaction for audit purposes. The compliance guide A5 will have details, but the SOP should mention the key forms, like the DG declaration.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "clap",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M24",
            "speaker_id": 456000,
            "reply_to": "M23",
            "text": "Excellent point. I'll add a checklist within that section of A2 referencing the required evidence from A5. Thanks.",
            "mentions": [
              254387
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2",
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M25",
            "speaker_id": 449944,
            "reply_to": "M20",
            "text": "My main concern is the data handover process in Appendix A of A2. It relies on an end-of-day email from the relocation coordinators. This could become a bottleneck. If an email is missed, we can't close the books for that day's jobs. We need a more robust process.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A2"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M26",
            "speaker_id": 333646,
            "reply_to": "M25",
            "text": "I agree. What if we define a shared folder where coordinators upload a standardized job completion form for each move? We could then check that folder at a set cut-off time, say 4 PM daily. That decouples us from relying on individual emails.",
            "mentions": [
              449944
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M27",
            "speaker_id": 267889,
            "reply_to": "M26",
            "text": "A shared folder sounds better. What information would be on that form?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M28",
            "speaker_id": 456000,
            "reply_to": "M27",
            "text": "That brings us to the minimum data set. I propose: Job ID, Client Name, Final Weight/Volume, List of Surcharges (with codes), and a scan of the signed delivery confirmation. Anything else essential?",
            "mentions": [
              267889
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M29",
            "speaker_id": 254387,
            "reply_to": "M28",
            "text": "We also need the DG declaration form scan if applicable. That's critical.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M30",
            "speaker_id": 449944,
            "reply_to": "M29",
            "text": "Yes. And the team lead's name for any queries. That list seems complete and actionable for the minimum set.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M31",
            "speaker_id": 333646,
            "reply_to": "M30",
            "text": "Okay, let's formalize this. We agree on the minimum data set required from operations as proposed by @456000, plus the DG form and team lead name. This will be captured via a standard form in a shared folder, with a 4pm daily cut-off.",
            "mentions": [
              456000
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D4"
            ],
            "reactions": [
              {
